VeridianOS: fix the remaining KWin compiler warnings

GCC reported, for the VeridianOS cross build (KWin 6.7.5, Qt 6.12, KF 6.30,
libei 1.6). Each change matches what upstream KWin master does, so it can
be dropped with the release that carries it:

- src/kcms/common/genericscriptedconfig.cpp:112: ignoring the [[nodiscard]]
  result of QFile::open. An unreadable config.ui now shows the existing
  "Error loading widget from %1: %2" label with the file error; before,
  QUiLoader::load() failed on the unopened file and the same label showed
  the loader's error instead.
- src/plugins/eis/eiscontext.cpp:161: four libei 1.6 events not handled in
  the switch (-Wswitch): EIS_EVENT_DEVICE_READY,
  EIS_EVENT_SEAT_DEVICE_REQUESTED, EIS_EVENT_TEXT_KEYSYM,
  EIS_EVENT_TEXT_UTF8. They fell through the switch and were dropped; they
  are now listed with the ignored events (this release has no text-input
  support for emulated input; master adds it).
- src/plugins/qpa/integration.cpp:96: QPlatformIntegration::RasterGLSurface
  is deprecated ("no longer used"). The case is removed; the default branch
  returns QPlatformIntegration::hasCapability(), which is false for it
  (qplatformintegration.cpp), as the case did.
- src/plugins/windowsystem/windowsystem.cpp:52:
  KWaylandExtras::xdgActivationTokenArrived() is deprecated since KF 6.19.
  requestToken() implements the deprecated request API; nothing in this
  stack calls KWaylandExtras::requestXdgActivationToken() (checked across
  every package built), and the token is served by xdgActivationToken(),
  which this plugin already implements. requestToken() is now empty, as in
  master.
- src/backends/drm/drm_output.cpp:761: unused variable 'wcg'; removed (it
  was computed and never read).
- src/backends/wayland/wayland_backend.cpp:649: unused variable
  'attributes' in an if-condition; the condition tests the pointer
  directly. Same branch taken.
- src/wayland/keyboard.cpp:217, src/wayland/inputmethod_v1.cpp:95:
  'waylandState' may be used uninitialized. The switch covers every
  KeyboardKeyState value, so it is always assigned; it is now initialized
  to WL_KEYBOARD_KEY_STATE_PRESSED like master, which the compiler can see.

